601 - Watchmen, on the Walls of Zion
 / 
Key: C
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 601
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
[C]Watchmen, on the walls of [F/C]Zion, [C]What O tell [Dm/A]us, of [C/G]the [G]night?
[C]Is the daystar now arising? Will the [Dm/A]morn soon [C/G]greet [G]our [C/G]sight?
[C/G]O'er your vision Shine [Dm/F]there [C/E]now [G/D]some [C/E]rays of light?
[C]O'er your vision [Dm/A]Shine there now [C/G]some [G]rays of [C/G]light?

Verse 2:
[C]Tell, O tell us, are the [Dm/A]landmarks
[C]On our voyage all [Dm/A]passed [C/G]by?
[C]Are we nearing now the [Dm/A]haven?
[C/G]Can we e'en [Dm/F]the [C/E]land descry?
[C/G]Do we truly See [Dm/F]the heavenly [C]kingdom nigh?
[C]Do we truly [Dm/A]See the heavenly [G]kingdom [C/G]nigh?

Verse 3:
[C]Light is beaming, day is [Dm/A]coming!
[C]Let us sound [F/C]aloud [Dm/A]the [C/G]cry;
[C]We behold the daystar [Dm/A]rising
[C/G]Pure and bright [Dm/F]in [C/E]yonder sky!
[C/G]Saints, be joyful; Your [Dm/F]redemption [C/E]draweth nigh;
[C]Saints, be joyful; [Dm/A]Your redemption [G]draweth [C/G]nigh.

Verse 4:
[C]We have found the chart and [Dm/A]compass,
[C]And are sure [F/C]the [C/G]land [Dm/A]is [C/G]near;
[C]Onward, onward we are [Dm/A]hasting,
[C/G]Soon the haven will appear;
[C/G]Let your voices Sound [Dm/F]aloud [G/D]your [C/E]holy cheer;
[C]Let your voices [Dm/A]Sound aloud [C/G]your [G]holy [C/G]cheer.
